      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I fixed this issue by **properly** baking the rotation in Blender instead of animating the root of the avatar in Unity. \nExported my animation from Unity to Blender using UMotion Pro and parented my armature to an empty object that spun so that I could use Bake Action to easily animate the spin.\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/666699982404976672/984169330302390302/blender_FyFMOY3k6M.mp4?size=4096\nSeems that before IK Beta, you could animate the avatars root and rotate it, which feels like a bug that I accidentally relied on.\n(i cannot delete post as it is 5+ votes)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-13T12:32:01.126Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "My AFK animation rotates the avatar root to spin in a circle. \nIt spins twice as much using the Beta IK, works as expected in Legacy.\nhttps://youtu.be/3SxTEddfOIk\n\nMy anim clip:\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/611291003344781388/952544976200425492/AFK_Roll.anim\n\nnakos",
